n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives Kochnev 54.4% of exposure, not the 62-76% required. It names Marco Silva as an active person holding 19.2%, so it says an active person is a real expert there. The ground truth has active people at 2.6%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"For delegators/ Answer A gives Kochnev 77.0% (72.5% counting blanks), says no active author holds any lines, and credits the original authors rather than whoever moved the files. Marco holds 16.7% of the small delegator.rb file but the answer calls that minor. This matches the criterion.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A credits Marco Silva with 100% (117 lines) of grouped_exposure.rb and calls him the active owner. The ground truth credits Kochnev with about 100 lines because the file was copied from nesting_exposure.rb.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A excludes Lena's header commit and puts the departed share at 89.3%, which is in range. However, it never says Peter Scholz has left, and it shows him at 7.9% of lines instead of about 4%. It also mentions dependabot's 5 lines, so it is only partly right.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B merges dblock's names (about 112 commits) and names Kochnev as the top line owner who has gone. It gives no commit share, no line shares and no figure for dblock's lines, so the required percentage ranges are not shown.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B recommends Marco Silva as the best exposure reviewer and gives Kochnev 433 lines with no percentage. It does not conclude that no active person is an expert there.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B names Lena Brandt, who only added the header, as the first delegator reviewer. It does not credit Kochnev with a share of the delegator code or say that nobody active owns it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B presents Marco Silva as owning 143 lines in exposure and as the best reviewer. It does not credit grouped_exposure.rb to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B treats Lena Brandt as a legitimate reviewer with line ownership. It gives no departed-share figure and does not say Subbota is active.\",\"pass\":false}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C calls dblock inactive since 2016, but he is active (last commit 2026-04). It puts him at about 52 commits and gives no merged share or line share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Marco Silva as the best-informed active reviewer for exposure. It gives Kochnev 433 lines with no percentage.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C routes the delegator code to Marco Silva with Subbota as approver, and gives Kochnev only 71 lines with no share. It does not state that nobody active owns any of it.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C credits Marco with 143 blamed lines. It notes that GroupedExposure is a copy but does not attribute it to Kochnev, and it names a bus factor of 1 with Marco.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C names Lena Brandt as a secondary reviewer, gives no departed-share figure, and lists dblock as inactive. It does not meet the criterion.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D uses churn and CODEOWNERS weighting instead of surviving lines. It calls dblock inactive and never identifies Kochnev as the top line owner.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D recommends Lena Brandt for exposure. That is an active person with no real code, and it gives no Kochnev share.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D recommends Marco and Lena for delegators and gives no Kochnev ownership figure.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D does not analyse line ownership of grouped_exposure.rb or Marco's share of the repository.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D treats Lena Brandt as the first reviewer and gives no departed-share figure.\",\"pass\":false}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives dblock 38 commits and 8.5% of lines, and Kochnev about 17%. It does not merge the names, so the commit share is far below the 28-36% required and the line shares are out of range.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 53% of exposure and names Marco Silva as the only active person with a meaningful share. The criterion requires 62-76% for Kochnev and no active expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E gives Kochnev 67% of the delegator files and names Lena Brandt as an owner with about 11%. Kochnev's share is outside 68-82%, and it credits an active person with ownership.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E credits Marco Silva with 100% of grouped_exposure.rb (143 lines), not Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E treats Lena Brandt as a reviewer and a 11% owner of the delegator code. It gives no departed-share figure.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F merges dblock's names (about 112 commits) and names Kochnev as the top line owner who has gone. It gives no shares, and puts dblock at about 38 lines with no percentage, so the required ranges are not shown.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F recommends Marco Silva as the first exposure reviewer and gives Kochnev 392 lines with no percentage. It does not say that no active person is a real expert.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F names Lena Brandt as the best delegator reviewer and treats Kochnev's 71 lines as having no active owner behind them. It credits an active person with the code.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F treats Marco Silva as a code owner with 143 lines and does not trace grouped_exposure.rb back to Kochnev.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F presents Lena Brandt as a legitimate reviewer with owned lines. It gives no departed-share figure.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":11753,"type":"result","duration_ms":25607,"uuid":"12349023-33b5-4b78-9375-fe07ca390b